rewritten-to-match
Same LZW decoder: a dictionary of byte strings where each entry is a copy of the previous code's string plus one byte (the reference's Vec<Vec<u8>> becomes one byte array with an offset and length per entry, the decoded text living in the same array after the dictionary; the clone and the output copies are array.moves), and the output is the strings in order. The encoder that prepares the input is the language's version (see Compress::LZWEncode's audit) and untimed, as in the reference; the equality test with the input runs in the checksum request. Stores are checked and undo-logged.
